  "year": 2025,
  "arxivId": "2505.16421",
  "abstract": "WebAgent-R1 is a novel end-to-end multi-turn reinforcement learning framework for training web agents. It addresses the challenges of long-horizon decision-making in dynamic web environments through dynamic context compression and parallel trajectory rollout. Experiments on the WebArena-Lite benchmark demonstrate significant improvements over existing methods, with success rates increasing from 6.1% to 33.9% for Qwen2.5-3B and from 8.5% to 44.8% for Llama3.1-8B.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "Imagine a web agent that can interact with a website like a human would, navigating through pages, clicking buttons, and filling out forms. <strong>WebAgent-R1</strong> is a framework that enables this by using <strong>end-to-end multi-turn reinforcement learning</strong> to train web agents. It learns from online interactions with web environments, guided by binary rewards that indicate task success.",
