    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The framework consists of two main components: <strong>dynamic context compression</strong> and <strong>parallel trajectory rollout</strong>. Dynamic context compression reduces memory overhead by simplifying earlier observations, while parallel trajectory rollout improves sampling efficiency by generating multiple trajectories in parallel. This allows the agent to learn from a diverse set of experiences and adapt to changing web environments.",
